scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: the-west-wing
run_id: 3
total_caught: 5
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 23
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 62.2
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    TEA tests cover config loading but not the distinction between NotFound and other
    error types. Dev implemented the pattern. Reviewer did not flag it.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented ServerError Display as #[error(\"server error\")] hiding\
    \ the inner String. Reviewer verified: \"ServerError Display hides internal details\
    \ \u2014 error.rs:17: #[error(\"server error\")] \u2014 the inner String is not\
    \ exposed in Display output. Verified good.\" TEA also wrote tests for CWE-209\
    \ coverage."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: "tenant field uses raw Option<String> instead
    of TenantId newtype" at cli.rs:19 and recommended using TenantId from axiathon-core.
    TEA wrote header injection tests (CWE-113) but did not specifically test for TenantId
    type usage.'
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [HIGH]: \"Missing workspace dependency declarations\
    \ for reqwest and toml\" \u2014 \"6 deps (clap_complete, comfy-table, csv, dirs,\
    \ reqwest, toml) use direct versions instead of workspace = true.\" Listed as\
    \ blocking required change."
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [HIGH]: \"RawConfig silently accepts and discards\
    \ unknown fields\" \u2014 noted the _ignored IgnoredAny pattern is a no-op and\
    \ that a user putting token in config would believe it's being read. Called it\
    \ a security concern."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...) in config tests. The reviewer flagged a different vacuous test (siem_client_rejects_token_with_newlines)
    but not this specific None || true pattern.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [LOW]: \"siem_client_rejects_token_with_newlines\
    \ test is vacuous\" \u2014 \"the test creates a client with a newline-injected\
    \ token and then does nothing with it (let _ = client). It doesn't verify the\
    \ token was sanitized.\" Recommended as strongly recommended fix #6."
